---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";
import { GITHUB } from "../utils/site";
const UPDATED = "October 15, 2026";
---

<Page title="Terms of Service" description="The terms for using the Airdrop over-the-air update service.">
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p>Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>
    <p>
      These terms govern your use of Airdrop, a hosted service that delivers over-the-air JavaScript and asset updates to
      React Native apps ("the Service"), including the API at <code>airdrop-api.guhcostan.dev</code>, the website and
      dashboard. By requesting access, using an app token or publishing an update, you agree to them on behalf of yourself
      or the organization you represent ("you").
    </p>

    <h2>1. The Service and early access</h2>
    <p>
      Airdrop is in early access: we onboard customers individually and features may change. The software development kit
      (SDK) and command-line tool are open source under the MIT license; these terms cover the hosted Service, not your use
      of that code.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Accounts and app tokens</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We issue app tokens scoped to your app. Keep them secret; you're responsible for activity under your tokens.</li>
      <li>Tell us promptly if a token may be compromised so we can revoke it.</li>
      <li>We strongly recommend enabling code signing (<code>airdrop init --sign</code>) so devices only accept updates signed with your private key, which we never receive.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Your content</h2>
    <p>
      You keep all rights to the bundles, assets and release notes you upload ("Your Content"). You grant us a limited
      license to store, process and deliver Your Content to your app's users solely to provide the Service. You confirm you
      have the rights to Your Content and that delivering it complies with the policies of Apple, Google and any store you
      distribute through. Airdrop only updates JavaScript and assets; you must not use it to download executable native code.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No malware, unlawful content, or content that infringes others' rights.</li>
      <li>No attempts to access other customers' data, probe or overload the Service, or bypass rate limits and plan limits.</li>
      <li>No reselling of the Service without a written agreement.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Plans, limits and fees</h2>
    <p>
      Plans and prices are listed on our <a href="/#pricing">pricing page</a> and are based on monthly active devices
      (distinct installs that check for updates in a calendar month, UTC) and storage. If your app exceeds its plan by more
      than 10%, publishing new updates is paused until you upgrade or the next month starts; devices keep receiving the
      updates already published. During early access, fees are agreed with you directly. We'll give at least 30 days' notice
      before changing the price of a plan you're on.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Availability and support</h2>
    <p>
      We work to keep the Service available and fast, but during early access it is provided without a service-level
      agreement unless one is agreed in writing (Enterprise). If the Service is unavailable, apps keep running the bundle
      already on the device. Support is provided through your onboarding contact and
      <a href={`${GITHUB}/issues`}>GitHub issues</a> for the SDK and CLI.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Data protection</h2>
    <p>
      Our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains what we process. For data about your app's users you are the
      controller and we process it on your behalf, only to provide the Service.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Ending the Service</h2>
    <p>
      You can stop at any time and delete your app and its data (<code>DELETE /v1/apps/:id</code> or by asking us). We may
      suspend or end access for breach of these terms, non-payment or to protect the Service or other customers, with notice
      where reasonably possible. On termination we delete your app's data as described in the Privacy Policy.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Disclaimers and liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by law, the Service is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind. You are responsible
      for testing the updates you publish. Neither party is liable for indirect or consequential damages, lost profits or
      lost data, and our total liability for any claim is limited to the fees you paid for the Service in the 12 months before
      the claim. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Changes and contact</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms; material changes will be announced to customers at least 30 days before they take effect.
      Questions: contact us through your onboarding email or the <a href="/#access">early-access form</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Page>
